skills:
  occ_skills:
    - { name: "Language: Dragonese", base: 98, per_level: 0, note: "Elven/Dragonese is the Changeling''s natural language, 98%. Half of all Changelings are also literate in it." }
    - { name: "Disguise", base: 45, per_level: 5, note: "+20%. Automatic." }
    - { name: "Impersonation", base: 52, per_level: 4, note: "+22%. The book names the Palladium skill Imitate Voices & Impersonation, which the catalog holds as two Rifts skills; this is the impersonation half." }
    - { name: "Imitate Voices & Sounds", base: 64, per_level: 4, note: "+22%. The voice half of Imitate Voices & Impersonation." }
natural_abilities:
  - name: "Shape Changing"
    description: "Assume the appearance of any humanoid creature, down to specific individuals and races, in one full melee (15 seconds). Height from three to ten feet (0.9 to 3 m), with mass varying only about thirty pounds, so small forms are fat and tall ones thin. Hair, fur, complexion, apparent age and sex all change at will. Cannot become an animal, insect or object, grow or remove limbs, tails or wings, or regrow a lost limb for a disguise. Attributes never change, and clothes do not change with the body."
  - name: "Superior Mental Endurance and Affinity"
    description: "The aura is too close to a human''s or an Elf''s to be conclusive, and the high M.E. makes psionic probes difficult."
  - name: "Salt Intolerance"
    description: "Eating salt causes nausea, stomach upset, gas and possibly vomiting for 1D4+2 hours. Changelings also tire easily and are more susceptible to disease."
  - name: "S.D.C. Mortal"
    description: "No natural A.R. and no M.D.C. - even in the guise of an M.D.C. creature the Changeling remains an S.D.C. mortal and needs M.D.C. armor, magic or a force field. Any body armor fits it, and Changelings love technology."
  - name: "Asexual"
    description: "No gender of its own; it can take a male or female form, or both."
restrictions:
  - "Changelings NEVER get bionics or major cybernetics unless absolutely necessary, as after losing a limb - mechanical limbs, even Bio-Systems, cannot transform with the body."
extraction_notes: |
  - Rifts Conversion Book One printed 82-83 (file p083-p084). The Rifts conversion of the Palladium Fantasy Changeling, which is the `changeling` row. A separate class because a variant cannot cross systems.
  - Attribute dice, hit points, P.P.E. 5D6 and the three +2 saves match the Palladium row. S.D.C. is "only those gained from O.C.C. and physical skills", so there is no pool bonus.
  - "+2 to save vs telepathic probes, mind control and Horror Factor" lands on `psionics`, `mind_control` and `horror_factor`, as on the Palladium row.
  - R.C.C. skills, which the Palladium row does not have: Elven/Dragonese 98%, Disguise +20% and Imitate Voices & Impersonation +22%. Rifts splits that last skill in two - Impersonation (Espionage, 30%) and Imitate Voices & Sounds (Rogue, 42%) - and both are granted at +22% rather than guessing which half the book meant. "50% are also literate" is on the language line rather than a grant.
  - occ_restrictions enumerates the O.C.C.s: every full conversion ''Borg (combat-cyborg, the Coalition strike trooper, the NGR and Free Quebec cyborg soldiers, and the South America 2 ''Borgs), both Crazies and every Juicer including the Maxi-Killer. A ''Borg, Crazy or Juicer imported after this names nothing here and is allowed until it is added.
  - Psionics: "Standard, same as humans", so no psionics block.
  - The book''s Size line prints "Seven feet (1.2 m)"; seven feet is 2.1 m, as its own opening paragraph says. Weight 180 to 250 pounds. Life span 250+ years.
  - The section-wide rule on printed 74 - a new arrival from the Palladium World picks up the regional language and two Modern W.P.s within weeks, then three Rifts skills from Communications, Pilot (basic vehicles), Technical and W.P. Modern after 2D4+4 months or one level, and one more language or skill every two levels - applies to a character who came from Palladium rather than one raised on Rifts Earth. It is not stored; the survey carries it.
