# Changeling

## Lore

Whether the Changelings began on the Palladium World is debated, for small hidden communities of them turn up across the Megaverse. On Palladium they are said to be a creation of the Old Ones and are hunted by every race except the Elves, who merely distrust them - because a Changeling can become anyone, perfectly, and legend blames them for murdering whole tribes in their sleep. A few thousand survive there, disguised among other peoples.

In their true shape they are thin, hairless, pale yellow humanoids seven feet tall. On Rifts Earth there are perhaps a dozen or two, most of them in the service of dimensional travelers; the Splugorth do employ them as assassins, bounty hunters, spies and slavers, though only a handful outside Atlantis have reached the rest of the planet.

**Alignment:** Any. Despite their reputation, Changelings can be good, noble and heroic.

**Average Life Span:** 250+ years.

## GM Notes

Every race is feared, and Elves are the nearest thing to an ally, but Changelings like to keep secret company among humans, Wolfen, D-Bees and other humanoids. A disguised Changeling is considered a D-Bee on Rifts Earth - when it is noticed at all.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'rifts-changeling');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'rifts-changeling';

